    <section id="privacy-10">
        <h2>10. Your mobile number and the first-order rule</h2>
        <ul><li>Your mobile number is a contact number: staff use it to reach you about your order. We only check that it looks like a Philippine mobile number (11 digits starting with 09); we do not send a code to verify it.</li><li>Your first order is paid online first (50% or the full amount). Our server decides whether an order is your first from your account, and only a payment confirmed by our payment provider (HitPay) counts.</li><li>So that the rule cannot be skipped, we compare the mobile numbers on your account with those of customers who already have a paid order. If your number matches another customer&#x27;s, your account still pays its first order online first. This never stops you from creating an account.</li></ul>
        <p class="muted" style="color:#91571C">Draft wording — to be confirmed by Melai Nuts.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="privacy-11">
        <h2>11. Security checks and sign-in protection</h2>
        <ul><li>Every sign-in attempt is counted by email address, IP address and device for 30 minutes. After 15 attempts, a security check (Cloudflare Turnstile) is needed before the next one. It never locks you out: a passed check always lets you try. The email, IP address and device ID are stored only as one-way hashes made with a secret key.</li><li>Cloudflare receives what it needs to run the security check (such as your IP address and browser details) under its own privacy policy.</li><li>App Check: the app proves to our servers that it is the genuine Melai Nuts app on a real device (Google Play Integrity or Apple App Attest). No personal data is added for this.</li><li>Password reset: the reset link in the email works once and expires; after the change, your other sign-ins are ended.</li></ul>
        <p class="muted" style="color:#91571C">Draft wording — to be confirmed by Melai Nuts.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="privacy-12">
        <h2>12. Working offline (staff and owners)</h2>
        <ul><li>What is kept on a staff or owner phone: the branch&#x27;s last inventory and dashboard figures; the e-receipts of the branch&#x27;s most recent orders (up to 300: items, quantities, prices, totals, payment method, order number, date, branch and, when the order has them, the customer&#x27;s name and contact number); notifications raised on the phone (connection lost or restored, changes synced, expired stock); a list of expired batches already announced (batch IDs only); and changes saved while offline, each with the staff account ID and the time.</li><li>Why: so the branch can keep selling, receiving and adjusting stock without a connection, show receipts offline, and send every change to our server once, without duplicates.</li><li>Where: only in the app&#x27;s private storage on that phone, not shared with other apps. Nothing stored on the phone can change what an account is allowed to do: our server checks every change again when it arrives.</li><li>How long: the saved copies of inventory, orders, e-receipts and notifications are erased when you sign out. Changes not yet sent stay on the phone, linked only to the account that made them, until they are sent or a staff member discards them; another person who signs in on the same phone cannot see or send them. After the server accepts a change, its record on the phone is deleted within 14 days.</li><li>Customers: if you buy at a branch counter, the staff phone may keep your e-receipt for the reasons above.</li></ul>
        <p class="muted" style="color:#91571C">Draft wording — to be confirmed by Melai Nuts.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="privacy-13">
        <h2>13. Loyalty cards and NFC</h2>
        <ul><li>What we keep about your card: a one-way hash of the card&#x27;s ID number (not the number itself), its short label (GK-XXXX-XXXX), its status (active, blocked or replaced), when and at which branch it was issued, and a history of when it was linked, blocked, unblocked or replaced and by which staff account. If you set a loyalty PIN, only a salted one-way hash of it is kept.</li><li>Taps on Melai Nuts card readers are logged (reader, time and result) to stop misuse.</li><li>Staff phones (NFC): after the staff member allows it with the &quot;Allow NFC&quot; button, a staff phone reads only your card&#x27;s ID number when you hold the card against it at the counter. It reads nothing else on the card, writes nothing to it, and the reader is on only while the card screen is open. The ID number is sent to our server to find your account and is not saved on the phone. The staff member&#x27;s choice is saved only on that phone and can be changed at any time in Settings &gt; Permissions.</li><li>Who sees it: only signed-in staff at the counter see the name and points of the card&#x27;s owner. The card&#x27;s ID number cannot be read back from what we keep.</li><li>How long: your card records are kept while your account is active and are deleted with your account (sections 5 and 7), except records we must keep by law.</li></ul>
        <p class="muted" style="color:#91571C">Draft wording — to be confirmed by Melai Nuts.</p>
